You have to switch them on. By default, video recording is set to `'off'`.

To enable video recording, you must configure the `video` option in your `playwright.config.ts` file. You can choose from the following modes:

*   **`'on'`**: Record video for each test.
*   **`'retain-on-failure'`**: Record video for each test, but remove all videos from successful test runs.
*   **`'on-first-retry'`**: Record video only when retrying a test for the first time.

Example configuration:

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';
export default defineConfig({
  use: {
    video: 'on-first-retry',
  },
});
```

Once enabled, video files will appear in your test output directory (typically `test-results`).

